      "representative_posted_date": "2026-05-26T04:00:00Z",
      "representative_length": 1951,
      "representative_excerpt": "Gambling activity, particularly sports betting, involves extremely high transaction volume with relatively small long-term margins. Taxing gross activity instead of true net winnings effectively creates phantom income that does not exist in reality. For example, a bettor who wins $500,000 and loses $500,000 during the year has not made a profit. Under the...",
